# Keeps `gcloud builds submit` from uploading history, Terraform state and local
# caches to Cloud Build. Without this file gcloud generates one from .gitignore
# and writes it into the checkout as an untracked file.
#
# The include below is not decoration and must not be dropped: a custom
# .gcloudignore REPLACES gcloud's default behaviour, so without it every
# gitignored-because-secret file in a working checkout — `.env.*`, a filled-in
# model-providers.json, generated Helm values — would ride into the uploaded
# source archive. .dockerignore does not help: it filters what reaches the
# build, long after the upload happened.
#!include:.gitignore

.git/
.github/
.claude/
**/.terraform/
**/tfplan
